---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About StackVerdict"
	description="Learn about our mission, software evaluation process, and editorial standards at StackVerdict."
	pubDate={new Date('October 01 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Welcome to <strong>StackVerdict</strong> — your trusted source for unbiased, hands-on reviews, side-by-side comparisons, and deep dives into modern developer tools, AI coding assistants, and SaaS software.
	</p>

	<h2>Our Mission</h2>
	<p>
		The modern software ecosystem moves extremely fast. With hundreds of new AI tools, IDE plugins, and productivity platforms launching every month, developers and tech teams waste valuable time trying to figure out which tools actually deliver on their promises.
	</p>
	<p>
		At StackVerdict, our goal is simple: <strong>cut through the marketing hype and provide honest, practical analysis</strong> to help indie hackers, software engineers, and engineering teams build their ideal tech stack with confidence.
	</p>

	<h2>How We Evaluate Tools</h2>
	<p>
		We don't just rehash feature lists from vendor homepages. Our review methodology is built on:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Real-World Testing:</strong> Deploying tools in actual production workflows and development environments.</li>
		<li><strong>Performance & Context Benchmarks:</strong> Testing speed, accuracy, context windows, and IDE latency.</li>
		<li><strong>Pricing Transparency:</strong> Evaluating free tiers, tier limitations, and total cost of ownership for solo developers vs. teams.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Editorial Independence</h2>
	<p>
		While StackVerdict participates in affiliate marketing programs (read our full <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a>), our opinions and rankings are strictly independent. Software companies cannot pay us for a positive review or higher placement on our listicles.
	</p>
</Layout>